# Root ignore rules for the whole workspace.
#
# READ THIS FIRST: this repository is NOT a git repository and must never
# become one (ADR 0003, founder constraint 2026-08-25; `.claude/settings.json`
# denies every git and gh command). There is no `.git` directory here, so
# nothing below is currently being enforced by git.
#
# This file is kept accurate anyway because it is a real, load-bearing manifest
# of "what in this tree is generated and must never be copied as if it were
# source". Three things actually read it or its shape today:
#   - `.prettierignore` and the ESLint config keep the same exclusions, so a
#     rule that drifts here tends to drift there too.
#   - backups/zips of D:/kd/wp (the founder's own backup procedure, since ADR
#     0003 means there is no remote) should skip exactly these paths.
#   - `/.dockerignore` mirrors most of it; the two are reviewed together.
# If the no-VCS decision is ever lifted, this file is already correct.
#
# Per-project ignore files are deliberately NOT used. In a pnpm workspace the
# root file governs every project, and splitting the rules across app/, admin/
# and website/ creates four places for the same rule to rot. Anything specific
# to one project is written below under a heading that names it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
#
# Every one of these is produced by `pnpm run build`, `vite build`,
# `next build`, or `tsc -b`. `dist/` alone is not enough: this workspace has
# 14 `*.tsbuildinfo` files (tsc's incremental cache, one per composite
# project) and three website-specific output directories.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test, lint and tooling caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
.eslintcache
.turbo/
.vite/
*.log

# app/frontend and admin/frontend: TanStack Router's own scratch directory.
# Note this is NOT `src/routeTree.gen.ts` - that file is generated too, but it
# is imported by `app.tsx` and must stay tracked (it is listed in
# `.prettierignore` instead, so it is never reformatted by hand).
.tanstack/

# website/ runs Playwright (`pnpm -F website test:e2e`) and Lighthouse
# (`test:perf`); both write result directories next to the project.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.lighthouseci/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and machine-local state
#
# `.secrets/` is the DESIGNATED local secret store (dev.env, dev key rings from
# scripts/gen-key-ring.mjs). It is machine-local by design and is also
# allow-listed in `.gitleaks.toml` for exactly that reason - the secret scanner
# exists to catch secrets OUTSIDE this directory.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.secrets/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Machine-local object-store data (P20 Unit U3 - the fs driver's default
# rootDir). Holds uploaded tenant CSVs and media; deliberately outside every
# guard's scan globs so tenant content is never scanned or committed.
.data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent / editor local state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Claude Code auto-memory is machine-local. Project knowledge that a fresh
# clone needs lives in .memory/decisions, lessons and research instead, and
# those ARE tracked.
.memory/auto/*
!.memory/auto/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# External reference repos reviewed under ADR 0012 (not part of WP)
#
# ~450 MB of Blastup + evolution-api, cloned under a scoped git exception for
# review only. Nothing under app/, admin/, website/, packages/, db/ or
# scripts/ imports from it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
demo/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT listed here on purpose
#
# Deploy image tarballs (~350 MB each) are written OUTSIDE this tree, to
# ../wp-deploy-artifacts, by infra/deploy/build-image.sh. They are not ignored
# here because they never appear here: `scripts/check-tree.ts` enforces the
# ADR 0014 top-level tree and would fail the gate on a new root directory.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
